### Describe the bug

This works:
```
	import static_image from './favicon.png?blur=1';
```

But this:
```
	let dynamic_image;
	let name = 'favicon';

	onMount(async () => {
		dynamic_image = (await import(`./${name}.png?blur=1`)).default;
	});
```

Is treated the same as:
```
	let dynamic_image;
	let name = 'favicon';

	onMount(async () => {
		dynamic_image = (await import(`./${name}.png`)).default;
	});
```

A few users have hit this in `vite-imagetools`: https://github.com/JonasKruckenberg/imagetools/issues/575

### Reproduction

https://github.com/benmccann/imagetools-575

### Steps to reproduce

`npm install` followed by `npm run dev`

Look in `src/routes/+page.svelte` to see two images imported. The dynamic import and static import should look the same, but they have different levels of blur because the query string is being dropped in the dynamic case.

